 **Speed control:** Frame interval = `(1/fps) / speedMultiplier`. Supported range: 0.25× (slow motion) to 8× (fast forward). Fast-forward is always available on every game: the phone HUD button, Select+R1, Tab, and the pause-menu speed chips all go through `EmulatorService.setSpeed` / `toggleFastForward`. Select+R1 is `LogicalKeyboardKey.gameButtonSelect` (the physical Select/View button), not `PadSlot.select` — see §4.5. A former Settings **Turbo Mode** switch could disable that; it is retired (`enableTurbo` in old JSON is ignored). **Turbo Speed** in Settings still sets the HUD/hotkey multiplier (default 2×).
 
+The native loop's sleep decision includes the time spent in the current
+iteration (core execution, achievement evaluation and presentation). Accumulators
+are still updated only at the next iteration start, so elapsed time is counted
+once. An overdue emulation deadline runs immediately; an overdue display tick
+alone waits for the next emulated frame. A refused lifecycle gate retains a
+full-frame backoff. `native/test/test_frame_pacing.c` covers these cases, PAL
+and explicit speed changes. This removes frontend oversleep; it cannot make a
+core whose execution exceeds the frame budget sustain full speed.
